---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { paperProfiles } from '../../../reading/paper-profiles';

const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
const href = (route: string) => `${base}${route.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Literature · Guided Reading"
  description="Source-faithful guides to foundational and research papers in electronic structure."
  current="reading"
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href={href('/reading/')}>Guided Reading</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span aria-current="page">Literature</span>
  </nav>

  <h1>Literature</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A literature guide helps you read the paper that changed the field without replacing it. The paper’s own problem, sequence, equations, evidence, and limits remain the organizing structure.
  </p>
  <p>
    Later clarification is marked as later clarification. For computational papers, guides reconstruct what the authors reported about the physical model, approximations, numerical representation, sampling, and calculated objects; unreported parameters remain unreported.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="density-foundations">
    <h2 id="density-foundations">The density-functional foundations</h2>
    <p>
      The first two papers form the original theorem-to-orbitals sequence. Hohenberg and Kohn establish why the ground-state density can carry an exact variational problem. Kohn and Sham then introduce auxiliary one-electron equations. Levy returns to the density variation itself and defines the universal functional by a constrained search that no longer requires every trial density to be the ground-state density of another potential.
    </p>
    <ol class="section-list source-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Hohenberg & Kohn · Inhomogeneous Electron Gas</h3>
        <p>{paperProfiles['hohenberg-kohn-1964'].citation} <a href={paperProfiles['hohenberg-kohn-1964'].sourceUrl}>Original source</a>.</p>
        <p class="item-summary"><strong>Why it matters.</strong> {paperProfiles['hohenberg-kohn-1964'].whyItMatters}</p>
        <p><strong>What to look for.</strong> {paperProfiles['hohenberg-kohn-1964'].lookFor}</p>
        <a href={href('/reading/literature/hohenberg-kohn-1964/')}>Read the Hohenberg–Kohn guide</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Kohn & Sham · Self-Consistent Equations</h3>
        <p>{paperProfiles['kohn-sham-1965'].citation} <a href={paperProfiles['kohn-sham-1965'].sourceUrl}>Original source</a>.</p>
        <p class="item-summary"><strong>Why it matters.</strong> {paperProfiles['kohn-sham-1965'].whyItMatters}</p>
        <p><strong>What to look for.</strong> {paperProfiles['kohn-sham-1965'].lookFor}</p>
        <a href={href('/reading/literature/kohn-sham-1965/')}>Read the Kohn–Sham guide</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Levy · Universal Variational Functionals</h3>
        <p>{paperProfiles['levy-1979'].citation} <a href={paperProfiles['levy-1979'].sourceUrl}>Original source</a>.</p>
        <p class="item-summary"><strong>Why it matters.</strong> {paperProfiles['levy-1979'].whyItMatters}</p>
        <p><strong>What to look for.</strong> {paperProfiles['levy-1979'].lookFor}</p>
        <a href={href('/reading/literature/levy-1979/')}>Read the Levy guide</a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="many-body-spectra">
    <h2 id="many-body-spectra">One-particle spectra and screened interactions</h2>
    <p>
      Density-functional theory is a ground-state reformulation. Hedin instead asks how an interacting system propagates an added electron or hole, how the electronic medium screens the Coulomb interaction, and how those coupled objects can become a controlled approximation.
    </p>
    <ol class="section-list source-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Hedin · One-Particle Green Function</h3>
        <p>{paperProfiles['hedin-1965'].citation} <a href={paperProfiles['hedin-1965'].sourceUrl}>Original source</a>.</p>
        <p class="item-summary"><strong>Why it matters.</strong> {paperProfiles['hedin-1965'].whyItMatters}</p>
        <p><strong>What to look for.</strong> {paperProfiles['hedin-1965'].lookFor}</p>
        <a href={href('/reading/literature/hedin-1965/')}>Read the Hedin guide</a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="literature-boundary">
    <h2 id="literature-boundary">Read the source and the Atlas together</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={href('/core/part-iv/')}>Core Part IV · Density Functional Theory</a> and <a href={href('/core/part-viii/')}>Core Part VIII · Excitations and Spectra</a> give the Atlas’s modern synthesis. These guides instead preserve what each paper argues in its own order, including historical notation and limitations that a modern textbook often reorganizes.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
